  "robert-g-edge": { name: "Robert G. Edge", role: "Honorary Member", photo: "",
    bio: `Robert Edge was elected president of the Atlanta Music Festival Association (AMFA) in 1972. Founded in 1910 to support the Metropolitan Opera’s annual tour stop in Atlanta, the AMFA had built a reserve fund of about $1.8 million by the time the Met stopped touring. It has since given The Atlanta Opera $70,000 or more every year for decades, more than $2.6 million in all.` },
