  "dr-thomas-n-guffin-jr": { name: "Dr. Thomas N. Guffin, Jr.", role: "Advisory Council", photo: "",
    bio: `Tommy Guffin’s mother, Betty, was a soprano, and both his parents helped keep professional opera going in Atlanta after the Metropolitan Opera’s tours ended in 1986. An accomplished operatic tenor himself, he made his career as an otolaryngologist caring for singers, and his office’s “wall of fame” holds headshots of dozens of famous singers he has treated.

Over the decades he has helped The Atlanta Opera in many ways, from administrative work to singing as a soloist and in the chorus, sometimes even slipping backstage mid-performance to help an ailing artist. He is a member of the Opera’s Advisory Council and a faithful donor.` },
