  "laurie-tossing": { name: "Laurie Tossing", role: "Mezzo-soprano", photo: "images/people/laurie-tossing.jpg", details: [["Mezzo-soprano in", "Twilight of the Gods, Turandot, The Marriage of Figaro, La traviata"]],
    bio: `Alto Laurie Tossing made her Atlanta Opera debut in 2002 in La rondine and had sung in almost thirty operas with the company by 2014. She calls the 2007 Turandot, the company’s first show at the Cobb Energy Centre, a career highlight.` },
  "jessica-wax": { name: "Jessica Wax", role: "Mezzo-soprano · Chorus Personnel Manager", photo: "images/people/jessica-wax.jpg", details: [["Mezzo-soprano in", "Twilight of the Gods, Turandot, La traviata"], ["Chorus Personnel Manager in", "Twilight of the Gods, Turandot, The Marriage of Figaro, La traviata"], ["Atlanta Opera debut", "The Pirates of Penzance, 2016"]],
    bio: `Jessica Wax is an Atlanta-based artist and has been performing with The Atlanta Opera since 2015. She has her master’s degree in vocal performance from Florida State University, and The Magic Flute will be her seventh Atlanta Opera Studio Tour.

Her favorite roles include Stephano in Romeo et Juliette, Fantine in Les Miserables, Wife in Stephen Sondheim’s Putting it Together, and Hansel in The Atlanta Opera Studio Tour of Hansel and Gretel.` },
